      <h2>About Spice Farm Tour (Kidichi)</h2>
      <p>Kidichi and Kizimbani spice farms offer immersive guided tours of Zanzibar&#x27;s legendary spice plantations — cloves, nutmeg, cinnamon, vanilla, cardamom, black pepper, turmeric, and ginger grown in traditional agroforestry systems. Expert guides explain cultivation, harvesting, and the historical spice trade that made Zanzibar the &#x27;Spice Island&#x27; and a global trade hub. Tours include tasting fresh spices, traditional hand-grinding demonstrations using mortar and pestle, and optional Swahili lunch featuring spice-infused dishes. The spice trade shaped Zanzibar&#x27;s history, architecture, and multicultural identity.</p>

